  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tom kha gai serves 4 and takes about 30 minutes. The soup is gentler than tom yum, with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "coconut milk",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "coconut-milk"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " cushioning the sour and spicy notes. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Galangal",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "galangal"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "lemongrass",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lemongrass"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " do most of the flavour work. This soup is a good weeknight option because it needs very little preparation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not boil the coconut milk hard once it goes in. A gentle simmer keeps the broth smooth and prevents it from splitting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
